---
// DRAFT answers: the client must review and approve them before launch.
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "Aren't these just superstitious practices?",
    answer:
      "Numerology, Tarot and Vastu are traditional systems of reflection and design rooted in Vedic thought. We use them as tools for self-understanding and more conscious choices, never to create fear or dependency.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do I need any prior spiritual knowledge?",
    answer:
      "None at all. Every session starts from the basics and is explained in simple, practical terms. All you need is an open mind and a question you'd like to explore.",
  },
  {
    question: "Will Vastu require major renovations to my home?",
    answer:
      "Rarely. Most recommendations are simple adjustments, such as the placement of objects, colours, light and the balance of elements, that work with the space you already have.",
  },
  {
    question: "How soon will I see results?",
    answer:
      "Everyone's journey is different. Many people feel greater clarity soon after a session; lasting change grows gradually as the guidance is applied in daily life.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can sessions be done online?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Numerology and Tarot sessions take place online via Google Meet. Vastu consultations can be done online using your floor plan.",
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="section section--sand">
  <div class="container faq-inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
    <h2>I Want to Begin, But…</h2>

    <div class="faq-list">
      {faqs.map((item) => (
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            <span>{item.question}</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <p class="faq-answer">{item.answer}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq-inner {
    max-width: calc(760px + var(--gutter) * 2);
    text-align: center;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.4rem);
  }

  .faq-list {
    margin-top: 48px;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .faq-item { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(30, 46, 32, 0.15); }

  /* The question row: the part you click */
  summary {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: 24px 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;               /* hides the default triangle */
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }   /* …also in Safari */
  summary:hover { color: var(--color-saffron-dark); }

  /* A "+" drawn with two thin lines; it turns into "×" when open */
  .faq-icon {
    position: relative;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    transition: transform 0.25s ease;
  }
  .faq-icon::before,
  .faq-icon::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 50% 0 auto;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--color-gold);
  }
  .faq-icon::after { transform: rotate(90deg); }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-icon { transform: rotate(45deg); }

  .faq-answer {
    max-width: 640px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #4f5a45;
  }
</style>